# What `pnpm run format:check` (RRR §9's prettier gate) must not look at.
#
# Prettier 3 reads BOTH `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore` by default, so
# `node_modules/` and `dist/` are already excluded by the `.gitignore` beside this
# file and are deliberately not repeated here.  What is left is the one committed
# file prettier must be told to leave alone.
#
# pnpm writes `pnpm-lock.yaml` itself, in its own style: flow mappings on one line
# (`engines: {node: ...}`), a blank line after `importers:` and after `packages:`.
# Prettier disagrees with about two thirds of the file — 953 of 1429 lines, measured
# — and would expand every `resolution:` into a four-line block.  Reformatting it
# would be undone by the next `pnpm install` that touches a dependency, which means
# the gate would go red on a change that has nothing to do with formatting, and
# every future dependency bump would carry hundreds of lines of reflow noise.  A
# generated file is formatted by its generator.
pnpm-lock.yaml
